  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building cohesive communities in Dnipropetrovsk Oblast</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To foster a conducive environment for early recovery in the war-affected communities of Ukraine, IOM will provide multisectoral individual-level and community-based support, especially in those communities that report higher rates of return. In order to maximize community resilience, the project foresees activities that reinforce the social fabric, through initiatives that promote community-based recovery, improve access to social services, and increase individuals&#x2019; self-reliance capacities, through the promotion of livelihoods and psychosocial wellbeing. To understand the needs and the vulnerabilities of the growing number of families and individuals returning to the Dnipropetrovska Oblast, the project will run IOM&#x2019;s assessment on the Conditions of Return, which will provide granular data on the vulnerabilities that stem from poor physical and social conditions in areas of return and will ultimately inform the intervention.</narrative>
  </description>
